# Skills Available for This Project

These skills are installed in `.claude/skills/` and invocable via the Skill tool.
Cursor agents should reference these when the trigger phrase matches the task.

## Planning & Execution

| Skill | Invoke As | Trigger |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| writing-plans | `power-skills-bundle:writing-plans` | Before implementing any multi-step task |
| executing-plans | `power-skills-bundle:executing-plans` | Running a written implementation plan |
| dispatching-parallel-agents | `power-skills-bundle:dispatching-parallel-agents` | 2+ independent tasks (e.g. build models + enums + fixtures in parallel) |
| using-git-worktrees | `power-skills-bundle:using-git-worktrees` | Starting a new feature branch |

## Implementation Quality

| Skill | Invoke As | Trigger |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| test-driven-development | `power-skills-bundle:test-driven-development` | Before writing any implementation code |
| verification-before-completion | `power-skills-bundle:verification-before-completion` | Before claiming a task is done |
| systematic-debugging | `power-skills-bundle:systematic-debugging` | Any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior |
| requesting-code-review | `power-skills-bundle:requesting-code-review` | After completing a feature, before merging |

## Code Review & Architecture

| Skill | Invoke As | Trigger |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| adversarial-python-review | `adversarial-python-review` | Pressure-test Pydantic models or httpx session design |
| python-project-review | `python-project-review` | Full codebase health check |

## MCP Development

| Skill | Invoke As | Trigger |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| mcp-builder | `mcp-builder` | Building `mcp_server.py` / FastMCP tools |

## Project-Specific Notes

- **Always** use `writing-plans` before implementing a new module
- **Always** use `test-driven-development` when building session.py, roster.py, audit.py
- **Always** use `verification-before-completion` before committing
- Use `mcp-builder` when implementing the 5 MCP tools (list_elections, describe_election, fetch_roster, fetch_turnout, run_audit)
- Use `adversarial-python-review` before finalizing `models.py` schema
